  <body>
    <SiteHeader />
    <main>
      <section class="page-header pillar-hero" style="--topic: rgba(241,94,74,0.16); --topic-fg: #d8412c;">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="breadcrumbs">
            <a href="/">Home</a><span>&#8250;</span>
            <a href="/seo">SEO</a><span>&#8250;</span>
            <a href="/seo/backlinks">Link Building</a><span>&#8250;</span>
            <span>Affiliate Marketing Posting Sites</span>
          </div>
          <span class="card-icon pillar-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
          <p class="eyebrow">Link building</p>
          <h1>{title}</h1>
          <p class="pillar-intro">{intro}</p>
          <PageByline />
          <figure class="posting-feature">
            <img src="/images/posting/affiliate-marketing-posting-sites.png" width="1200" height="630" alt={title} loading="eager" />
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="content-body">
        <div class="container article-shell">
          <div class="prose pillar-body">
            <p class="prose-lede">Affiliate publishing splits into four tiers, and where you can land a byline depends on whether you have real numbers or just opinions.</p>
            <p>The marketing and SEO blogs do not take open guest posts. The affiliate and monetisation blogs take case studies with real numbers. The networks take education for their own blogs. The blogging sites are open. The list of 100 is below, grouped by tier.</p>

            <h2 id="tier">Pick your tier first</h2>
            <figure><table>
              <thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Examples</th><th>How you get in</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Marketing &amp; SEO blogs</td><td>Backlinko, Ahrefs, Semrush, HubSpot, Search Engine Journal, Neil Patel</td><td>Not open guest posts. Original data, a case study, or expert commentary on a live SEO story</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Affiliate &amp; monetisation blogs</td><td>Authority Hacker, Niche Pursuits, Smart Passive Income, Adam Enfroy, Diggity Marketing</td><td>Real case studies with revenue numbers, tested tactics, tool comparisons</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Affiliate networks &amp; tools</td><td>Impact, Awin, ShareASale, ClickBank, Rakuten, Cloudways, Thrive Themes</td><td>Contributed education for their blog; how partners actually use the platform</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Blogging &amp; small-business</td><td>ProBlogger, Blogging Wizard, Blogging Tips, Startup Bonsai, Make a Living Writing</td><td>Practical guides, first-hand experience, monetisation breakdowns</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table></figure>

            <h2 id="metrics">What the metrics mean</h2>
            <figure><table>
              <thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>What it is</th><th>How much it matters</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Domain Rating (DR)</td><td>Ahrefs' 0 to 100 score for a whole site's backlink profile</td><td>A useful filter, not a verdict</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Domain Authority (DA)</td><td>Moz's equivalent 0 to 100 score</td><td>Same idea as DR</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Page Authority (PA)</td><td>Moz's score for one specific page</td><td>Matters once you know which page your post will live on</td></tr>
                <tr><td>URL Rating (UR)</td><td>Ahrefs' score for one specific URL</td><td>Same purpose as PA</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Monthly Traffic</td><td>Estimated organic visits per month</td><td>The most honest signal that a link will be seen</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table></figure>

            <div class="callout"><p><strong>Here is the deal:</strong> affiliate marketing is one of the most link-spammed niches on the web, and Google knows it. A placement on a site with a real audience and case-study data is worth far more than a link on a made-for-links blog that has not posted since 2020.</p></div>

            <h2 id="list">The 100 sites</h2>
            <p>Domain Rating, Domain Authority, Page Authority, URL Rating and estimated monthly traffic. Every domain was checked live in September 2026; shut-down and made-for-links sites were replaced with active publications. Metrics are third-party estimates and shift over time.</p>
            <figure><table>
              <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Website</th><th>DR</th><th>DA</th><th>PA</th><th>UR</th><th>Monthly traffic</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                {SITES.map((s) => (
                  <tr><td>{s.n}</td><td>{s.site}</td><td>{s.dr}</td><td>{s.da}</td><td>{s.pa}</td><td>{s.ur}</td><td>{s.traffic}</td></tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table></figure>

            <h2 id="pitch">The pitch that works</h2>
            <ol>
              <li><strong>Lead with the numbers.</strong> "We took this site from $0 to $4,200/month in 11 months, here is the breakdown" earns the read.</li>
              <li><strong>Show the work.</strong> Screenshots of real dashboards, a traffic graph, a documented timeline. Editors reject claims they cannot verify.</li>
              <li><strong>Pitch the section.</strong> "For your case-study series" or "for the SEO tactics coverage" shows you read the blog.</li>
              <li><strong>Bring the assets.</strong> A spreadsheet, a step-by-step process, a spend-vs-return table.</li>
              <li><strong>Match the format.</strong> Marketing blogs want a data-led argument. Affiliate blogs want a full case study. Blogging sites want a practical how-to.</li>
              <li><strong>Disclose the affiliate relationship</strong> behind any tool or program you write about.</li>
            </ol>
            <div class="callout"><p><strong>The test:</strong> would an editor run this if you had nothing to sell? If yes, pitch it. If it exists only to place a link, it goes in the bin.</p></div>

            <h2 id="mistakes">What not to do</h2>
            <ul class="check-list">
              <li>Buy links from "affiliate blogs" that quote a flat per-post price. That is the exact footprint Google penalises here.</li>
              <li>Pitch a "what is affiliate marketing" explainer. Every site has ten.</li>
              <li>Send a case study with no screenshots and no numbers.</li>
              <li>Put exact-match anchors ("best affiliate program") on links back to your offer.</li>
              <li>Use AI-generated "passive income" content with no real results behind it.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="callout"><p><strong>Bottom line:</strong> in affiliate marketing, one placement on a respected blog with a real income report or case study beats a dozen links from thin "make money online" sites. Use the traffic column and recent posting activity to find the real ones.</p></div>
          </div>

          <aside class="article-toc">
            <h4>On this page</h4>
            <ul>{toc.map((item) => (<li><a href={`#${item.id}`}>{item.text}</a></li>))}</ul>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div id="faq"><Faq items={faqs} /></div>

      <section class="section section-alt">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="cta-panel" style="text-align: center; max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto;">
            <h2>Want us to run the outreach?</h2>
            <p>We shortlist the affiliate and marketing blogs that carry weight, package your case-study data, write the pitches and place them. No link farms, no PBNs, no risk.</p>
            <div class="hero-actions" style="justify-content: center; margin-top: 0;">
              <a href="/services" class="button">View services</a>
              <a href={whatsappUrl('Hi SERP Mentor, I would like help with affiliate marketing guest posting and digital PR.')} class="button-secondary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                <i class="fa-brands fa-whatsapp" aria-hidden="true"></i> WhatsApp
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <SiteFooter />
  </body>
</html>
